From 5bc17725b0542d8ac37fa989bc1c86afe651a103 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tad <tad.keller@pm.me>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 09:46:08 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 16/19] libcamera: software_isp: debayer_egl: Add NV12 output

The Android camera HAL streams NV12. For NV12 output the Bayer shader
renders RGB to an intermediate texture, from which two programs write the
Y and the interleaved UV plane of the output buffer, each rendered as an
ARGB8888 image of a quarter of the plane's width: four bytes per fragment.
UV is the average of each 2x2 block, by one bilinear fetch. Full range
BT.601, as the CPU debayer's NV12 output. NV12 uses the CPU debayer's tight
stride, which buffers from the platform allocator have.

Also centre the scaled image on the output so that what doesn't fit is
cropped evenly on both sides instead of on the right and bottom, and
compute the statistics on the centre window of the input, where the CPU
debayer computes them, instead of its top left corner.
